 "text": "County Commission - McKenzie County, ND\nYou are using an outdated browser. Please upgrade your browser to improve your experience.\nSkip to content\nSkip to navigation\nSite map\nOfficial government website\nQuick top menu links Jobs\nEvents\nAction toolbar\nAnswers\nPayments\nReport Issue\nTranslate\nTranslate language select\nSelect language Afrikaans Albanian Amharic Arabic Armenian Azerbaijani Basque Belarusian Bengali Bosnian Bulgarian Catalan Cebuano Chichewa Chinese (Simplified) Chinese (Traditional) Corsican Croatian Czech Danish Dutch English Esperanto Estonian Filipino Finnish French Frisian Galician Georgian German Greek Gujarati Haitian Creole Hausa Hawaiian Hebrew Hindi Hmong Hungarian Icelandic Igbo Indonesian Irish Italian Japanese Javanese Kannada Kazakh Khmer Korean Kurdish (Kurmanji) Kyrgyz Lao Latin Latvian Lithuanian Luxembourgish Macedonian Malagasy Malay Malayalam Maltese Maori Marathi Mongolian Myanmar (Burmese) Nepali Norwegian Pashto Persian Polish Portuguese Punjabi Romanian Russian Samoan Scottish Gaelic Serbian Sesotho Shona Sindhi Sinhala Slovak Slovenian Somali Spanish Sundanese Swahili Swedish Tajik Tamil Telugu Thai Turkish Ukrainian Urdu Uzbek Vietnamese Welsh Xhosa Yiddish Yoruba Zulu\nSearch\nMcKenzie County, ND\nMenu\nPrimary menu links\nCommunity\nDepartments\nBoards\nServices\nNews\nContact\nMcKenzie County, ND\nCounty Commission\nMembers\nCounty Commission Meetings\nBid and RFP/RFQ Notices\nCounty Boards\nPast Commissioners\nContact\nErica Johnsrud Auditor\n(701) 444-3616 Ext. 3\nejohnsrud@co.mckenzie.nd.us\nPowers and Duties\nPursuant to ND Century Code 11-11-11, the McKenzie County Board of Commissioners holds significant authority and responsibility in overseeing the county’s operations. They manage fiscal affairs, supervise county officers and ensure proper financial audits. The board controls county property, constructs and maintains roads and bridges, levies taxes and regulates public utilities. Additionally, they handle countywide services such as garbage collection, public safety and election precincts. The commissioners also manage county infrastructure projects, participate in community development programs and ensure the submission of financial records from various county boards and committees.\nHelpful\n-->\nShare\nFacebook\nTwitter\nEmail\n-->\nSize\n+\nReset\na\n−\nWelcome\nAbout\nCommunity\nNews\nEvents\nJobs\nEngage\nConnect\nFeedback\nHelp\nServices\nContact\nDirectory\nSitemap\nPowered by\n1 --> Get answers\nMy services\nMake a payment\nReport an issue\n1 -->\nSelect question type\nCorrectional Facility\nProperty and Housing\nBuilding Codes and Zoning\nJobs\nGeneral Government\nClose window\nSearch Site\nSearch\nClose window",
